cmu-autocompressor-cannot-fit = Hold the CPR compressor in your active hand and stay beside the patient.
cmu-autocompressor-no-skill = You need corpsman-level medical training to fit the CPR compressor.
cmu-autocompressor-invalid-patient = The CPR compressor only fits a resuscitable human patient.
cmu-autocompressor-remove-armor = Remove the patient's outer clothing or armor before fitting the CPR compressor.
cmu-autocompressor-no-power = The CPR compressor has insufficient battery charge.
cmu-autocompressor-fitting = You begin fitting the CPR compressor to { $target }.
cmu-autocompressor-started = { CAPITALIZE(THE($device)) } starts compressions on { $target }.
cmu-autocompressor-stopped = { CAPITALIZE(THE($device)) } stops compressions.
cmu-autocompressor-battery-low = The CPR compressor signals low battery, shuts down and detaches.
cmu-autocompressor-already-running = A CPR compressor is already providing CPR. Remove it before performing manual CPR.
